    "摩洛哥山羊皮，烫金最衬的底子" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Morocco goatskin — no ground shows gold better"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tafilete de cabra: ningún fondo luce mejor el dorado"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Maroquin de chèvre — nul fond ne porte mieux la dorure"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "モロッコ革の山羊皮。金箔押しがいちばん映える下地"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "모로코 염소가죽, 금박이 가장 잘 받는 바탕"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "摩洛哥山羊皮，烫金最衬的底子"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "摩洛哥山羊皮，燙金最襯的底子"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "摩洛哥革（morocco）为山羊皮，细粒面，最宜显金；小牛革（calf）光滑少纹，为十七至十九世纪英国精装主流。" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Morocco is goatskin: close-grained, the best ground for gold. Calf is smooth and lightly figured, the mainstay of English fine binding from the seventeenth to the nineteenth century."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El tafilete es piel de cabra de grano fino, el mejor fondo para el oro; el becerro, liso y de poca veta, fue la base de la encuadernación fina inglesa entre los siglos XVII y XIX."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le maroquin est une peau de chèvre au grain serré, le meilleur fond pour l'or ; le veau, lisse et peu marqué, domine la reliure anglaise de qualité du XVIIe au XIXe siècle."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "モロッコ革（morocco）は山羊皮で、細かい粒面をもち、金がもっとも映える。仔牛革（calf）は滑らかで紋が少なく、十七〜十九世紀のイギリス精装本の主流だった。"
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "모로코 가죽(morocco)은 염소가죽으로, 결이 곱고 금박이 가장 잘 산다. 송아지가죽(calf)은 매끈하고 무늬가 적어 17~19세기 영국 고급 제본의 주류였다."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "摩洛哥革（morocco）为山羊皮，细粒面，最宜显金；小牛革（calf）光滑少纹，为十七至十九世纪英国精装主流。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "摩洛哥革（morocco）為山羊皮，細粒面，最宜顯金；小牛革（calf）光滑少紋，為十七至十九世紀英國精裝主流。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
